 "parsed": {
  "count": 2,
  "rationale": "The stages run in strict sequence, so the attack is stopped if every technique at any single stage is blocked. Recon cannot be blocked because internal_reconnaissance has no blocking control. Each other stage has exactly two techniques, and each technique is blocked by different controls, so emptying a stage takes two controls. For example, patch_struts (or waf) plus email_filtering (or security_awareness) blocks both foothold techniques. One control is not enough: every technique has its own blockers, so a single control removes at most one technique per stage and every stage keeps an open path."
 },
